    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="37d0f287-7984-5c39-a8b9-7d060aaa6948" activityNameId="5adc3354-ae2f-5406-9f1b-11b1cb2ee553" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Railway track, with overpass construction, double track</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Railway track, with overpass construction, double track
This inventory includes the construction of an overpass structure. The double-track overpass construction is 11 metres wide and 1000 metres long. The total area is 14,000m2 for a double track with overpass construction. The information on material requirements was approximated with the information on the construction of a railway bridge. 
The inventory also includes the rails, concrete sleepers, safety systems and traction current system according to SBB (pers. comm., SBB, 2024).

According to SBB, the service life is 94 years, the same as for a bridge, whereby the service life of the rails is 25 years and that of the railway sleepers 40 years. After that, refurbishment or new construction is due. Maintenance, refurbishment or dismantling were not taken into account in these inventories.; UUID:3f0401dd-f30d-3992-9fb8-a8ee07038625
The inventory includes all the materials, energy and transport necessary for constructing a double track railway overpass. Excluded are maintenance and disposal
Location: Data apply to construction in Switzerland. 
Technology: Average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: based on literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3f0401dd-f30d-3992-9fb8-a8ee07038625.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
